  "measurement_bounds": [
    "HTTP statistics are deltas between successful scrapes of each observed API process; activity before its first scrape is excluded",
    "Intervals spanning a process restart/counter reset are excluded; unobserved requests during such intervals are not reconstructed",
    "p50/p95 are containing Prometheus histogram bucket bounds, not exact quantiles or interpolated point estimates",
    "HTTP durations measure API request handling, not GPU inference task latency; all traffic on observed replicas is included",
    "Database counters aggregate the database; PostgreSQL wait samples are periodic observations, not wait-time durations",
    "Runtime-role visibility of other roles' activity may be redacted; WAL statistics can include other databases on the same cluster",
    "GPU utilization/memory include all workloads visible on each GPU, including unrelated tenants; no GPU process inventory is queried",
    "Database statistics, metrics and GPU probes finish at different times; each source includes its own elapsed time",
    "Polling, metrics aggregation and sampling themselves consume some control-plane/database capacity",
    "All selected samples are fully contained in the exact benchmark window; API counter deltas cover only first-to-last successful scrapes in this stream segment, not the entire benchmark",
    "Primary HTTP counters exclude the secondary Pod APIs; PostgreSQL samples include both Pods; H100 utilization includes unrelated co-tenants",
    "Twenty logical inference devices means four H100s plus sixteen distinct Blackwell MIG instances, not twenty equivalent full GPUs",
    "Primary and secondary worker-origin attribution requires separately collected per-worker before/after snapshots; HTTP request counts are not unique durable accepted-task counts",
    "This is one collector segment of a benchmark spanning a handoff; counter deltas are NOT bridged from the old collector to the new collector",
    "The new collector segment contains zero completion deltas if primary completions finished before its first scrape; do not infer zero benchmark-wide completions from that segment"
  ],
